Route optimization v2 is feature-complete, it's just bugs and tuning from here - call it 1 engineer-week of remaining effort. So the choice is really:

- Ship offline mode -> launch moves to late June or later
- Cut offline mode -> mid-May holds

If we cut something, offline is the one. Route optimization is already customer-visible in the dashboard demos, and pulling it now would be more disruptive to what we've promised. My take: offline goes to v3.1.

Cheers, Dev

On 2026-04-01, Jonas Eklund wrote:
> offline mode honest sizing: full offline (cached routes + manifests, edits queued locally, conflict resolution on reconnect) is ~6 engineer-weeks. that's me plus ravi for most of it, and the conflict-resolution piece is genuinely hard, it eats entire days and spits out edge cases. we would not start until the P1 burn-down is done anyway, so add another 2 weeks of calendar. it does not fit in mid-may. fwiw.

